{"name":"Evil Cigar","hex":"#522000","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"evil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Intending to harm; malevolent.","Morally corrupt."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Moral badness; wickedness; malevolence; the forces or behaviors that are the opposite or enemy of good.","Something which impairs the happiness of a being or deprives a being of any good; something which causes suffering of any kind to sentient beings; harm; injury; mischief."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/evil"},{"term":"cigar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cylinder of tobacco rolled and wrapped with an outer covering of tobacco leaves, intended to be smoked.","The penis. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cigar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Evil","blocks":[{"text":"Evil, as a concept, is usually defined as profound immorality, and it is related to acts that cause pain and suffering to others."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Demon._A_miniature_from_the_Georgian_manuscript_of_the_12th_century.jpg/330px-Demon._A_miniature_from_the_Georgian_manuscript_of_the_12th_century.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evil","wikidata":"Q15292"},{"title":"Cigar","blocks":[{"text":"A cigar is a rolled bundle of dried and fermented tobacco leaves made to be smoked. Cigars are produced in a variety of sizes and shapes. Since the 20th century, almost all cigars are made of three distinct components: the filler, the binder leaf which holds the filler together, and a wrapper leaf, which is often the highest quality leaf used. Often there will be a cigar band printed with the cigar manufacturer's logo. Modern cigars can come with two or more bands, especially Cuban cigars, showing Limited Edition bands displaying the year of production."}],"image":"https://thumb